                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "40467540",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197977551896",
                            "num_reviews": 3,
                            "playtime_forever": 13,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 13,
                            "last_played": 1519851839
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you like Deadbolt then you probably like Haste Heist. The gameplay is quite similar. The only big difference is that in Haste Heist you only sneak without attacking your enemies. So you try to finish levels without getting noticed. Therefore you sneak and hide in the shadow or behind objects. You also can run. But this produces sound as in Mark of the ninja and your enemy will hear you. \n\nI only played a short time but already have the feeling that this game will keep me interested much longer. This is usually not the case for most new games. If I will change my mind then I will change this review. Hence if you still read this review you know I still like the game.\n\nFurthermore the pixel graphics are very welcoming and nice. All in all this game feels very polished and I can recommend it to fans of 2d stealth games where you have to be cautious in order to finish the levels",
